### Description

Initiate an approval for a fast file transfer. This API only creates an approval task and runs a full pre-check on the parameters. **No file is transferred.** Once the approval is granted, Job executes it automatically as the creator of the task.

Before calling: the caller must have the permission to perform fast file transfer in the target resource scope, as well as the permissions on the source hosts, third-party file sources, execution accounts and target hosts. If the pre-check fails, an error is returned and no approval task is created.

{% include '_generic_v4_approval_flow.md.j2' %}

### Request Parameters

#### Body Parameters

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| bk_scope_type | string | Yes | Resource scope type. Options: `biz` (business), `biz_set` (business set) |
| bk_scope_id | string | Yes | Resource scope ID, corresponding to `bk_scope_type`, that is the business ID or the business set ID |
| approval_channel | string | No | Approval channel. Options: `IMATE` (IMate approval channel). The default channel configured on the server is used when omitted. Only the channel enum can be specified; the channel address and secret always come from the server configuration |
| task_name | string | No | Custom job name, at most 512 characters. Generated by the system when omitted |
| file_source_list | array | Yes | Source file list, cannot be empty |
| file_target_path | string | Yes | Target directory on the destination hosts |
| file_target_name | string | No | File name on the destination hosts. The source file name is kept when omitted |
| account_alias | string | No | Alias of the execution account on the destination hosts. Provide either `account_alias` or `account_id`; `account_id` wins if both are given |
| account_id | long | No | ID of the execution account on the destination hosts. Provide either `account_alias` or `account_id`; this one wins if both are given |
| execute_target | object | Yes | Distribution target |
| transfer_mode | int | No | Transfer mode. Options: 1 (strict mode, fails when the target path does not exist), 2 (force mode, creates the target path when missing and overwrites files with the same name). Defaults to 2 |
| download_speed_limit | int | No | Download speed limit in MB. No limit when omitted |
| upload_speed_limit | int | No | Upload speed limit in MB. No limit when omitted |
| timeout | int | No | File transfer timeout in seconds. Defaults to 7200, valid range 1-259200 |
| callback_url | string | No | Callback URL invoked after the job finishes, at most 1024 characters. Job calls it once the released job completes |
| rolling_config | object | No | Rolling execution config. Rolling execution is disabled when omitted |
| start_task | boolean | No | Whether to start the job immediately after the approval is granted. Options: `true` (start immediately, the default), `false` (only create the job instance without starting it) |

##### file_source_list[] element

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| file_list | array | Yes | Source file paths, each element being a file path string |
| file_type | int | No | File source type. Options: 1 (server file), 2 (local file), 3 (third-party file source file). Defaults to 1 |
| account_alias | string | No | Alias of the execution account on the source hosts. Provide either `account_alias` or `account_id`; required for a server file |
| account_id | long | No | ID of the execution account on the source hosts. Provide either `account_alias` or `account_id`; required for a server file |
| execute_target | object | No | Hosts holding the source files; required for a server file |
| file_source_id | long | No | Third-party file source ID. Provide either `file_source_id` or `file_source_code`; required for a third-party file source file |
| file_source_code | string | No | Third-party file source code. Provide either `file_source_id` or `file_source_code`; required for a third-party file source file |

##### execute_target and file_source_list[].execute_target

The distribution target `execute_target` and the source hosts `file_source_list[].execute_target` share the same structure:

{% include '_generic_v4_execute_target.md.j2' %}

**Note:** Hosts and containers cannot be mixed in one execution. When the distribution target contains dynamic groups or topology nodes, the actual number of destination objects is resolved again at release time and may differ from the moment of initiation; the approval ticket highlights this explicitly.

{% include '_generic_rolling_config.md.j2' %}

### Request Parameters Example

- POST

```json
{
    "bk_scope_type": "biz",
    "bk_scope_id": "2",
    "approval_channel": "IMATE",
    "task_name": "push-config-with-approval",
    "file_source_list": [
        {
            "file_list": [
                "/tmp/REGEX:[a-z]*.txt"
            ],
            "file_type": 1,
            "account_alias": "root",
            "execute_target": {
                "host_list": [
                    {
                        "bk_host_id": 10001
                    },
                    {
                        "bk_cloud_id": 0,
                        "ip": "127.0.0.1"
                    }
                ]
            }
        },
        {
            "file_list": [
                "testbucket/test.txt"
            ],
            "file_type": 3,
            "file_source_id": 1
        },
        {
            "file_list": [
                "testbucket/test2.txt"
            ],
            "file_type": 3,
            "file_source_code": "testInnerCOS"
        }
    ],
    "file_target_path": "/data/release/",
    "file_target_name": "app.conf",
    "account_id": 1000,
    "execute_target": {
        "host_list": [
            {
                "bk_cloud_id": 0,
                "ip": "127.0.0.2"
            }
        ],
        "dynamic_group_list": [
            {
                "id": "asdo8gojhasdfskft7pr5"
            }
        ],
        "topo_node_list": [
            {
                "id": 1000,
                "node_type": "module"
            }
        ]
    },
    "transfer_mode": 2,
    "download_speed_limit": 100,
    "upload_speed_limit": 100,
    "timeout": 1000,
    "callback_url": "https://example.com/job/callback",
    "rolling_config": {
        "type": 1,
        "execution_mode": 1,
        "mode": 1,
        "expression": "1 5 10 100%"
    },
    "start_task": true
}
```

